To modify existing code so that it also trims all white spaces, you'll need to know the context in which you're operating—whether this is a string in a programming language or something else. Here, I'll assume you're working with a string in a common programming language. I'll provide examples in Python, JavaScript, and Java.

### Python

If you have a string and you want to trim all white spaces from both the beginning and end of the string:

```python
# Original string
