        <input type="text" id="user-input" placeholder="Type your message..." />
        <button id="send-btn">Send</button>
    </div>

    <script src="chat.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

### Step 2: Load and Use the Model

Create a `chat.js` file to manage the conversation logic:

#### chat.js
```javascript
document.getElementById('send-btn').onclick = async () => {
    const inputField = document.getElementById('user-input');
    const userMessage = inputField.value.trim();

    if (!userMessage) return;

    addMessage(userMessage, 'user');

    inputField.value = '';

    // Load the model and make a prediction
    try {
        const model = await transformers.load('Xenova/blenderbot-400M-distill');

        const output = await model.generate(userMessage, {
            max_new_tokens: 60, // You may adjust this limit as necessary
        });

        const responseMessage = output.join('');
        addMessage(responseMessage, 'bot');
    } catch (error) {
        console.error("Error loading model:", error);
        addMessage("Sorry, something went wrong.", 'bot');
    }
};

// Function to add a message to the chat log
function addMessage(text, sender) {
    const chatLog = document.getElementById('chat-log');
    const messageContainer = document.createElement('div');
    messageContainer.className = `message ${sender}`;
    messageContainer.textContent = text;
    chatLog.appendChild(messageContainer);
    chatLog.scrollTop = chatLog.scrollHeight;
}
```

### Notes:

- **Loading Time**: The first time you run this, `transformers.js` will have to load a model, which may take some time. Ensure that you handle this by providing feedback to the user that something is loading.
- **UI Enhancements**: You might want to further style the chat interface or add more features like saving conversation histories.
- **Performance**: This setup is primarily for learning and prototyping. For production purposes, you may need additional infrastructure for performance optimization.
- **Error Handling**: Ensure that you adequately handle errors, such as issues loading models or network failures, to give the user feedback if something goes wrong.

With this setup, you can interact with the BlenderBot model using a simple chat interface. Adjust the styles and features to suit your needs as you further develop your application.

