Here is an example implementation of a VHDL UART transmitter:

```vhdl
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity uart_transmitter is
    port (
        input_clk      : in std_logic;
        input_word     : in std_logic_vector(7 downto 0);
        start_transmit : in std_logic;
        output_tx      : out std_logic
    );
end entity uart_transmitter;

architecture rtl of uart_transmitter is
    signal clk_divider : integer := 0;
    signal transmit_reg : std_logic_vector(9 downto 0);
    signal transmitting : std_logic := '0';

begin

    process(input_clk)
    begin
        if rising_edge(input_clk) then
            if start_transmit = '1' then
                transmitting <= '1';
                 transmit_reg <= "01111111110" & input_word & '0';
                 clk_divider <= 0;
            else
                if transmitting = '1' then
                    if clk_divider = 0 then
                        output_tx <= transmit_reg(0);
                        transmit_reg <= '0' & transmit_reg(10 downto 1);
                        clk_divider <= [CONFIGURABLE_DIVIDER_VALUE_HERE];
                    else
                        clk_divider <= clk_divider - 1;
                        output_tx <= '0';
                    end if;
                else
                    output_tx <= '0';
                end if;
            end if;
        end if;
    end process;

end architecture rtl;
```

This code demonstrates a basic UART transmitter in VHDL. You can customize the `CONFIGURABLE_DIVIDER_VALUE_HERE` constant to set the desired clock divider value. The transmitter is started by setting the `start_transmit` signal high for one cycle.

Please note that this code is a simplified example and may require further modifications based on your specific requirements and the exact UART protocol you are implementing.

